#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/components/documentation-dialog.tsx:644
msgid "documentation.comparisons.baselineDescription"
msgstr "The baseline is the last available close on or before the nominal window start. Year to date starts from December 31 of the prior year. The summary percentage is value-weighted: total change divided by total baseline value, not an average of ticker percentages."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/components/documentation-dialog.tsx:545
msgid "documentation.performance.contributionDescription"
msgstr "The contribution shown for an asset or class is its unrealized P&L divided by the entire portfolio's invested cost. It answers how many percentage points that item adds to the portfolio's open result; it is not the item's own return percentage."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/components/performance/value-card.tsx:51
msgid "performance.valueHint"
msgstr "The gap between the two lines is the open result: value above cost is gain, below is loss. In {currency}."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/components/score-documentation.tsx:343
msgid "documentation.score.priorityDescription"
msgstr "The grade multiplier times the cooldown ramp. Priority decides who is filled first and how close to target a cheque takes them; it never lowers the target itself."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/components/contribution-plan-documentation.tsx:533
msgid "documentation.contribution.exampleLargeDescription"
msgstr "The large-book impact is {largeImpact}, so a minimum slice is R$ 5,000. Two thousand reais stays in one name; N = 2 only from about R$ 7,500."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/components/score-documentation.tsx:283
msgid "documentation.score.valuationSignalDescription"
msgstr "The log distance between fair value and price, so half and double the fair value weigh the same. Mispricing inside ±{deadZone} is treated as valuation noise, and a cheap USD asset must also clear the FX spread and IOF. A missing fair value or price means no signal."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/components/documentation-dialog.tsx:392
msgid "documentation.positions.fxResult"
msgstr "The open result in the display currency therefore includes the FX move since each purchase. FX result isolates that part: cost at today's rate minus cost at the trade-date rates. Trades still without a trade-date rate convert at today's rate until you fill them from Transactions."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/components/documentation-dialog.tsx:494
msgid "documentation.performance.drawdownDescription"
msgstr "The percentage distance of the compounded return index from its previous peak. Maximum drawdown is the deepest such decline."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/components/documentation-dialog.tsx:426
msgid "documentation.performance.monthlyDescription"
msgstr "The performance page uses Modified Dietz so deposits and withdrawals do not masquerade as investment return. Each month is calculated separately and then compounded."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/components/contribution-plan-documentation.tsx:239
msgid "documentation.contribution.intro"
msgstr "The planner turns a contribution amount into suggested slices. The score still ranks who deserves capital; this method decides how many names that cheque can meaningfully move, and how much any one of them may take. Nothing is recorded until you register the trade."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/components/documentation-dialog.tsx:600
msgid "documentation.comparisons.dailyPercent"
msgstr "The portfolio percentage is that change divided by yesterday's comparable value, including cash. It is not the same as each ticker's native-currency return, and it is not the open result against moving-average cost."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/components/score-documentation.tsx:357
msgid "documentation.score.pipelineNextV2"
msgstr "The rule ladder then blocks, trims, or scores the relative gap times the priority."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/components/score-documentation.tsx:435
msgid "documentation.score.field.trimRelativeHint"
msgstr "The same band as a share of the adjusted target. The tighter of the two applies."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/components/score-documentation.tsx:250
msgid "documentation.score.introV2"
msgstr "The score answers how strongly an asset should compete for the next contribution. It is the share of the asset's valuation-adjusted target that is still missing, times its priority: 40% means 40% of the target is missing at full priority. Positive values are buy candidates, zero means skip, and a negative value is a trim signal. Thresholds below are yours to tune and persist with the account."

